<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Deliberately empty.

  There was a `keychain-access-groups` entry here, and it broke the app: simulator builds are
  unsigned (CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED is NO for iphonesimulator, so the app can run without a
  developer account), an unsigned build is granted no keychain access group, and every
  SecItemAdd then failed with errSecMissingEntitlement - which the app noticed only as
  "signing in returns you to the sign-in screen".

  A keychain access group is only needed to SHARE the keychain with an app extension or a
  sibling app. Muraka has neither: its session lives in its own default group, which needs no
  entitlement at all.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
